{% block how_it_works %}
## How it works

The arms, the population, the unit guard and the window are those of
[`get_ab_test`](/docs/tools/get-ab-test). Each path's events are numbered from its
start (by timestamp, then the stream's order); a cell `(event, step)` is 1 for a
path whose `step`-th event is `event`, and `(path_end, step)` is 1 for a path with
fewer than `step` events. An arm's value is the share of its paths, which on the
stream's paths is the number [`step_matrix_data(max_steps,
diff=...)`](/docs/widgets/step-matrix) shows for that arm. With an `assignment`
table, a silent path is in the denominators and has ended at step 1.

Every cell is a 0/1 per-path quantity over every path of the arm, so its delta is an
effect of the assignment, tested with the pooled z-test and a Newcombe interval. A
cell is tested when its pooled support (paths with the event at the step, and paths
without it) reaches `min_support`; the tested cells form one family adjusted with
`correction` (Benjamini-Hochberg by default), and the verdict reads the adjusted
p-value, as in [`get_ab_transitions`](/docs/tools/get-ab-transitions). The intervals
are per cell, not simultaneous.

Cells are not independent: a path that reaches `checkout` one step earlier moves
the `checkout` cells of two steps, and a path one event longer or shorter moves a
`path_end` cell (`path_end` at step k counts the paths with fewer than k events).
Under `horizon`, a path ends with the last event of its window, not when the user
left. Read the screen as
"where the paths of the two arms part", and confirm one hypothesis as the declared
metric of a new test.

Steps count from each path's start. To compare the steps around an event, cut the
paths first with [`truncate_paths`](/docs/data-processors/truncate-paths), on a
pre-exposure event; there is no `path_pattern` or `anchor` here. Step 0 (the
synthetic `path_start`) is not a cell.

On `load_ab_test()` with `max_steps=8`, 92 cells are tested and 14 differ; the
strongest is `quick_add` at step 7 (`+4.62 pp`, an event the control arm does not
have, flagged `one_arm_only`), and `add_to_cart` is lower in the treatment arm at
every step from 3 to 8 (the treatment's `quick_add` replaces it).

